title: Pre-test polish sweep — typography overhaul + objectFit + video cache + cross-fade reorder + tsup ESM-only
summary: |-
  Five-item polish pass before owner begins manual testing. (1) TYPOGRAPHY: Cormorant Garamond → Inter (UI-optimized variable sans, was hard to read in dense chrome per owner feedback). Body 15px/1.45, sidebar items 12→13, toolbar buttons 12→13, badge labels +1-2px, font smoothing antialiased on Retina. Updated getInlineHTML to preload Inter from Google Fonts. (2) renderVideo HONORS objectFit: defaults to 'contain' (aspect-preserved letterbox) instead of stretching; 'cover' and 'fill' implemented; falls back to fill when source dims unreadable. (3) MODULE-LEVEL VIDEO CACHE: BrowserVideoFrameProvider's video elements moved to module-level VIDEO_CACHE keyed by resolved URL; dispose() now only removes listeners, never aborts the in-flight 87MB MOV fetch. Workspace-app's mount cascade no longer wastes bandwidth re-downloading. Runtime-verified: ERR_ABORTED count 5→3 (remaining 3 are normal Chrome Range fragments at page close). New evictFromCache export for media-delete flows. (4) CAPTION CROSS-FADE REORDERED: buildPhraseDeltas moved fade-in from [start-fadeF, start] to [start, start+fadeF] so touching phrases don't overlap. Eliminates the 2-frame cross-fade that produced the false-bug 'captions stacking' report. Existing docs need re-transcribe to pick up. (5) TSUP CJS WARNING FIX: split cli.ts + mcp.ts entries into ESM-only configs (binaries are ESM, .cjs would crash on import.meta.url anyway). Library index.ts keeps ESM+CJS. Build is now warning-free. All 1212 tests pass. Runtime verification on a fresh studio confirms typography lands (Inter at 15px body, 1.45 line-height), video paints, captions display singly at frame 86, dropdown + ruler + letterbox intact.</summary>
  <parameter name="symbols_touched">["#workspace-app", "#inline-app", "#atelier-studio", "#canvas-panel", "#browser-video-frame-provider", "#video-renderer", "#caption-builder"]
