learnings:
  - Module-level singletons keyed by URL are the right cache scope for browser media (HTMLVideoElement, HTMLImageElement) when consumers have short lifecycles relative to media downloads. Per-consumer caches force redundant fetches; module-level survives consumer disposal cycles.
  - 'tsup''s `format: [''esm'', ''cjs'']` blindly builds both formats even for entries that use ESM-only features (import.meta.url). Split entries by binary vs library role: binaries that use ESM-only features should be ESM-only configs; library entries that need require() compat keep dual.'
  - Caption cross-fades that overlap on the SAME frame range produce visible 2-frame 'stacking' artifacts (~66ms at 30fps) where both captions render at intermediate opacity. Move the fade-in INSIDE the phrase window to sequence cleanly without overlap, instead of pre-fading.
